+## 1.2.0 — DRAFT, proposed 28 August 2026, NOT RATIFIED
+
+A focused amendment to the maturity and lifecycle policy for the portfolio AI
+assistant. **Nothing else changes.**
+
+**Changed**
+
+- **§49.1** — the assistant is authorised as a *narrow, optional feature* rather
+  than *"only as a narrow, optional beta"*. Stable public release is permitted
+  once ADR-recorded graduation criteria are met, the gate is green, and the
+  owner approves. The previous wording made "beta" a permanent condition of the
+  authorisation, which §46 meant no exception record could legitimately lift.
+- **§49.1** — two obligations added, both permanent and neither waivable by
+  graduation: a **truthful capability disclosure** that survives the removal of
+  any maturity label, and a prohibition on **silent degradation**.
+- **§49.6** — retitled *Feature maturity labels and graduation*. Labels are
+  required **while work is experimental** rather than indefinitely, with a
+  six-condition graduation mechanism requiring criteria recorded **before**
+  launch, reproducible evidence, a green gate, re-verified security, privacy,
+  accessibility, performance and cost obligations, retention of the capability
+  disclosure, and explicit owner approval. Adds a **regression** clause: a
+  graduated feature that stops meeting its criteria is fixed or relabelled.
+- **§48 Track C** — retitled from *"Instructor-required AI assistant beta"* to
+  *"Portfolio AI assistant as a client-ready, reusable product"*. A one-off
+  external requirement is no longer part of the product's permanent governance
+  identity. Adds an explicit evaluation-set requirement and a reusability
+  expectation. **No existing Track C requirement is removed or weakened.**
+- **§10** — the assistant's ADR trigger is "before its first public release and
+  again before any change of maturity status" rather than "before public beta".
+- **§52** — adds a v1.2.0 adoption checklist; the completed v1.1.0 checklist is
+  retained as §52.1.
